{
  "//": "CHAIN REACTION - tap a mote to detonate it. Every mote the blast touches detonates too. Set off all five.",
  "//engine": "Each mote is its own 1-count particle system, because a JSON document has no way to reduce across the particles of one system - and no way to write a variable outside the system being looped. Naming each mote separately is what makes 'did any neighbour reach me' expressible at all.",
  "//layout": "Motes sit ~60px apart and the blast reaches 58 + 9 = 67px, so any mote can ignite its nearer neighbours. At 75px spacing the chain never propagates and the game looks broken rather than hard.",
  "//limits": "Four neighbour tests do not fit in one 32-token expression, so each mote splits them across two accumulators (na, nb) and combines them the next frame. Chain propagation therefore advances one hop every two frames.",
